# sum_of_two_values:
# CSES 1640, Sum of Two Values (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1640), in our own
# words: a list of numbers and a target x; the pairs of two different places whose
# numbers sum to x. NARROWED from CSES's task, which prints the places of one such
# pair or says IMPOSSIBLE: we ask for the number of pairs of places i < j with the sum
# x, which is 0 exactly when CSES says IMPOSSIBLE and which, unlike a pair of places,
# the problem's definition fixes. The input is the binary natural x
# (corpora/library/binary/natural) and a Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of
# binary naturals; the answer is a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's fourth
# batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: for each place, the later numbers are
# walked, counting those that sum with its number to x, and the counts of all places
# are added. Its reading compares about n squared / 2 pairs; the replacement the
# family asks for is to sort the numbers and move two pointers in from both ends,
# counting the runs of equal numbers where they meet the target, in about n log n
# steps, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion consumes the finite list of
# numbers or of the numbers after one place; the branches that a Scott boolean
# discards are never read. The program calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V
# by the soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of
# Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an answer, P
# ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's
# theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and applying
# both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ target head
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self items found
        . items found
          λ other rest
          . self rest (merge_binary_equality (merge_binary_plus head other) target (merge_binary_increment found) found)
      )
  )
λ pairs_with
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ target
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self items found
        . items found λ head tail. self tail (pairs_with target head tail found)
      )
  )
λ pairs_from
. (λtuple. tuple λtarget values. pairs_from target values binary_zero)
λ sum_of_two_values
. export sum_of_two_values
